From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: touchscreen: add NT36523N report parser tests

Add a small parser for the normalized 65-byte touch reports emitted by the
Novatek NT36523N.  Keep the parser independent of SPI, input, DRM, firmware
loading and allocation so the hardware driver can consume only completely
validated reports.

Classify the controller's ESD and watchdog signatures before interpreting
contact records. Reject malformed active IDs, duplicate slots and
coordinates outside the configured raw range, and commit the result only
after the entire report has passed validation.

Exercise the format with synthetic KUnit reports, including every truncated
length, contact states and ID boundaries, both extended-pressure bytes,
fault signatures and output atomicity. This deliberately does not add a
transport or enable the controller on any board yet.
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig              |  20 ++
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile             |   2 +
 .../novatek-nt36523n-report-test.c              | 349 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 .../touchscreen/novatek-nt36523n-report.c       | 113 ++++++++
 .../touchscreen/novatek-nt36523n-report.h       |  50 ++++
 5 files changed, 534 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek-nt36523n-report-test.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek-nt36523n-report.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek-nt36523n-report.h

